    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Social/Emotional:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is shy, clingy, or fearful around strangers; shows several facial expressions (happy, sad, angry, surprised); looks when you call her name; reacts when you leave; smiles or laughs when you play peek‑a‑boo. "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Language/Communication:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " makes a lot of different sounds like \"mamamama\" and \"bababababa\"; lifts arms up to be picked up. "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cognitive:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " looks for objects when dropped out of sight; bangs two things together. "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Movement/Physical:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " gets to a sitting position by herself; moves things from one hand to the other; uses fingers to \"rake\" food toward himself; sits without support. [S3]"
     }
